1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,900
All right, these are the 11 players who'll move on to the final stage.

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:21,260
Oichi Fukatsu, Leon Sook, Toi Kachita, Junosuke Nakano, Yudai Hasegawa, Kensho Soda, Mamoru Izumi, Esaku Otomo, Akinori Kanida, Soichiro Tachibana.

3
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:21,680
Sir!

4
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,680
And last but not least...

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,260
Sorry, Shun, can you grab that?

6
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:35,120
Yeah, sure.

7
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,120
I did it.

8
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:42,340
I made the final cut, Shun!

9
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:43,940
Final stage of assessment!

10
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:45,320
That means I'm almost there!

11
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:46,720
Way to go!

12
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:48,880
I still can't believe it!

13
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:50,000
So close!

14
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:52,320
You'll ace this test, I know it.

15
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:56,620
My stakes are high since I taught you how to play.

16
00:00:57,440 --> 00:00:59,440
I'm counting on you to raise my stock.

17
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,120
I'll do my best!

18
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:03,420
Thanks, Shun.

19
00:02:37,671 --> 00:02:40,211
The final stage will commence in 30 minutes.

20
00:02:41,951 --> 00:02:44,511
Hey! You guys want to chat?

21
00:02:45,191 --> 00:02:48,131
Um, no pressure. I mean, just if you feel like it.

22
00:02:48,411 --> 00:02:50,831
I figured since there are 11 who made the cut,

23
00:02:51,231 --> 00:02:54,791
then that means the final stage is going to be an 11-on-11 match.

24
00:02:55,151 --> 00:02:57,871
So it'll be all of us against another 11, right?

25
00:02:58,051 --> 00:03:03,891
Then, uh, I was thinking that maybe we should get to know each other a little better since we're on a team.

26
00:03:03,891 --> 00:03:08,051
Uh, really?

27
00:03:08,831 --> 00:03:09,891
What's up with you?

28
00:03:09,991 --> 00:03:12,851
It took a lot of courage to stand out here and ask you guys that!

29
00:03:14,911 --> 00:03:15,351
Otomo?

30
00:03:15,731 --> 00:03:18,311
I don't feel like being alone until the final stage starts.

31
00:03:18,791 --> 00:03:19,351
Let's chat.

32
00:03:19,851 --> 00:03:23,511
I'd like to know your thoughts on love, and the origin of the word itself.

33
00:03:23,531 --> 00:03:24,011
Good idea.

34
00:03:24,751 --> 00:03:26,171
And I kind of like you both.

35
00:03:26,691 --> 00:03:26,971
Oh?

36
00:03:27,311 --> 00:03:28,871
Uh, yeah, me too.

37
00:03:31,091 --> 00:03:32,271
Hey, count me in.

38
00:03:33,891 --> 00:03:41,031
All righty, then.

39
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:45,391
Um, want to play truth or dare?

40
00:03:45,471 --> 00:03:47,211
I just say you wanted to talk when you've got nothing!

41
00:03:48,271 --> 00:03:48,671
Fine.

42
00:03:49,271 --> 00:03:50,151
I'll start it.

43
00:03:50,531 --> 00:03:52,811
Everyone say what your favorite playing style is.

44
00:03:53,231 --> 00:03:55,371
Like, what kind of passes you want to receive.

45
00:03:57,531 --> 00:03:58,411
What's all that?

46
00:03:58,491 --> 00:04:01,591
Not sure, but I'm guessing they are trying to come up with a plan.

47
00:04:01,931 --> 00:04:02,551
That's good.

48
00:04:02,551 --> 00:04:07,331
So, yeah, those are the kind of passes I prefer.

49
00:04:07,811 --> 00:04:10,791
Uh, it's weird how picky you all are.

50
00:04:11,171 --> 00:04:12,071
Look who's talking!

51
00:04:13,211 --> 00:04:14,951
We all want to get signed, don't we?

52
00:04:15,931 --> 00:04:16,371
Obviously.

53
00:04:17,711 --> 00:04:20,991
To be honest with you guys, I think this is going to be my last chance.

54
00:04:21,571 --> 00:04:22,731
To go pro, at least.

55
00:04:23,731 --> 00:04:24,091
Hmm.

56
00:04:24,091 --> 00:04:29,951
Nah, come on, you're exaggerating.

57
00:04:30,351 --> 00:04:30,891
Mine too.

58
00:04:32,511 --> 00:04:33,431
I'm not dumb.

59
00:04:33,511 --> 00:04:34,511
I know what level I'm at.

60
00:04:35,091 --> 00:04:37,231
We've got to ace this if we want to make the team.

61
00:04:37,531 --> 00:04:38,491
And that won't be easy.

62
00:04:39,791 --> 00:04:41,731
My dudes, we're the losers on the field.

63
00:04:41,731 --> 00:04:49,631
I don't want to join my high school soccer team, play three years, and then ditch it, like everyone else.

64
00:04:49,991 --> 00:04:51,211
That's where we're at.

65
00:04:51,571 --> 00:04:53,271
But that's not where I want to be.

66
00:04:54,051 --> 00:04:56,711
So I'm going to change it, no matter what it takes.

67
00:04:56,711 --> 00:05:06,011
Of course, Tajibana doesn't have to worry about any of that, since he's going to get promoted to his club's youth team regardless.

68
00:05:06,371 --> 00:05:07,031
Yeah, right.

69
00:05:07,671 --> 00:05:08,111
Sorry.

70
00:05:08,651 --> 00:05:10,731
Haven't improved as a player in quite a while.

71
00:05:11,571 --> 00:05:14,831
The home club I grew up in isn't exciting or challenging at all anymore.

72
00:05:15,591 --> 00:05:17,851
I'm just losing my competitive edge in general.

73
00:05:20,151 --> 00:05:20,891
It's fine.

74
00:05:21,171 --> 00:05:23,691
I came here today to try snapping myself out of it.

75
00:05:23,691 --> 00:05:27,691
If I don't go pro, my life's over.

76
00:05:28,311 --> 00:05:28,911
I'm done.

77
00:05:32,551 --> 00:05:33,391
That's wild.

78
00:05:33,711 --> 00:05:36,291
I've never given much thought to whether or not I'll go pro.

79
00:05:36,671 --> 00:05:38,851
I play because I love the game, that's all.

80
00:05:39,671 --> 00:05:41,111
You guys are the best.

81
00:05:41,951 --> 00:05:42,731
I mean that.

82
00:05:42,791 --> 00:05:45,651
I've never played at such a high level in my entire life.

83
00:05:47,051 --> 00:05:51,471
I don't see a single loser on this team.

84
00:05:51,471 --> 00:05:54,171
And I'm not smart enough to lie to you.

85
00:05:54,671 --> 00:05:56,051
What I'm saying is legit.

86
00:05:56,151 --> 00:05:56,931
You're all awesome.

87
00:05:57,231 --> 00:05:59,171
I can't wait to play soccer with you.

88
00:06:01,871 --> 00:06:04,911
Sorry for the wait.

89
00:06:05,191 --> 00:06:06,491
Here are your final opponents.

90
00:06:07,351 --> 00:06:08,471
Allow me to introduce...

91
00:06:08,471 --> 00:06:14,671
The Tokyo City Espirion Youth Team.

92
00:06:15,691 --> 00:06:16,791
See you on the field.

93
00:06:17,391 --> 00:06:18,471
Have a good match.

94
00:06:18,951 --> 00:06:20,351
What's that manager thinking?

95
00:06:20,811 --> 00:06:22,031
It's so messed up.

96
00:06:22,251 --> 00:06:22,471
What?

97
00:06:22,771 --> 00:06:23,851
Oh, seriously?

98
00:06:24,471 --> 00:06:24,891
Hey!

99
00:06:25,171 --> 00:06:26,591
What do you think you're doing, huh?

100
00:06:27,271 --> 00:06:27,711
Really?

101
00:06:28,271 --> 00:06:30,871
These guys are on a whole other level of physique and skills.

102
00:06:31,431 --> 00:06:32,531
It's not fair.

103
00:06:32,851 --> 00:06:35,031
How are we supposed to showcase our skills against them?

104
00:06:35,031 --> 00:06:41,411
You're saying you can't play against players who are stronger than you?

105
00:06:43,751 --> 00:06:47,611
The fact is, you're trying to prove that you deserve to be one of them.

106
00:06:48,151 --> 00:06:50,211
This is the perfect chance to do just that.

107
00:06:51,071 --> 00:06:52,331
So show us what you got.

108
00:06:53,271 --> 00:06:55,191
It makes a lot of sense if you think about it.

109
00:06:56,331 --> 00:06:57,591
This is ridiculous.

110
00:06:57,591 --> 00:06:59,811
I mean, get real.

111
00:06:59,811 --> 00:07:00,291
Babies.

112
00:07:00,511 --> 00:07:02,511
So this is the Espirion Youth, huh?

113
00:07:04,451 --> 00:07:07,691
I saw them play in the final of last year's J Youth Cup.

114
00:07:08,571 --> 00:07:11,211
The skill on display was beyond anything I was expecting.

115
00:07:11,751 --> 00:07:14,151
It was way above the level of regular high school soccer.

116
00:07:15,351 --> 00:07:18,471
I have dreamt for so long to one day play soccer on that level.

117
00:07:18,471 --> 00:07:27,371
I have an ambition, you see.

118
00:07:36,051 --> 00:07:36,531
Oh.

119
00:07:37,051 --> 00:07:38,271
And one more thing.

120
00:07:38,931 --> 00:07:41,791
At some point during the game, I'll have something to tell you all.

121
00:07:42,591 --> 00:07:46,451
It won't be an instruction or anything like that, but I expect your full attention.

122
00:07:46,451 --> 00:07:54,911
The crowd is still buzzing.

123
00:07:55,771 --> 00:07:57,031
It's hard to concentrate.

124
00:07:57,511 --> 00:07:58,651
Let's win this!

125
00:08:00,351 --> 00:08:00,831
Win.

126
00:08:02,691 --> 00:08:03,911
Howie's right, you guys.

127
00:08:04,471 --> 00:08:05,391
We can win this.

128
00:08:06,391 --> 00:08:08,871
I've seen a bunch of their members in the Under-15 League,

129
00:08:09,231 --> 00:08:11,251
and most of them are first years in high school.

130
00:08:12,431 --> 00:08:14,751
And that means they're only one year above us.

131
00:08:14,751 --> 00:08:18,071
So I believe we have a better chance than we thought.

132
00:08:20,051 --> 00:08:20,491
Fukuda.

133
00:08:22,371 --> 00:08:23,471
What's up, Akutsu?

134
00:08:24,071 --> 00:08:24,931
I want to play.

135
00:08:25,391 --> 00:08:27,131
Is it possible for you to put me on the team?

136
00:08:29,651 --> 00:08:30,911
Where's this coming from?

137
00:08:31,591 --> 00:08:31,991
Exactly!

138
00:08:32,391 --> 00:08:33,411
So quit crying!

139
00:08:33,851 --> 00:08:36,851
We're gonna beat those jerkwads, and then they'll have no excuse!

140
00:08:36,851 --> 00:08:38,911
They'll have to sign all of us up!

141
00:08:39,811 --> 00:08:41,651
There seems to be a misunderstanding.

142
00:08:42,131 --> 00:08:44,691
I don't think you really get who we are, do you?

143
00:08:45,311 --> 00:08:49,131
Our best bet is a 3-5-2 formation.

144
00:08:49,671 --> 00:08:51,791
Let's have Aoi and Kaneda as the two up front.

145
00:08:52,371 --> 00:08:53,391
I can play in the pocket.

146
00:08:53,951 --> 00:08:54,291
Aoi.

147
00:08:54,551 --> 00:08:55,671
Can I play on the right?

148
00:08:56,251 --> 00:08:56,731
Sure!

149
00:08:56,871 --> 00:08:57,711
Whatever you want!

150
00:08:58,851 --> 00:09:00,351
Hasegawa is holding midfielder.

151
00:09:00,551 --> 00:09:01,031
That cool?

152
00:09:02,451 --> 00:09:04,831
You all good with me commanding the back line?

153
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:05,731
That's great.

154
00:09:06,251 --> 00:09:08,531
I'd like the defenders to limit how much they go forward,

155
00:09:08,851 --> 00:09:10,011
and just focus on defense.

156
00:09:10,271 --> 00:09:10,691
Sound good?

157
00:09:11,851 --> 00:09:12,871
Aw, yeah!

158
00:09:13,211 --> 00:09:14,391
Let's get to it!

159
00:09:14,391 --> 00:09:21,591
Are they still working out their plan?

160
00:09:21,931 --> 00:09:23,431
Come on, hurry it up!

161
00:09:23,551 --> 00:09:24,071
Hey, man!

162
00:09:24,251 --> 00:09:25,791
What happened to your cleats?

163
00:09:26,391 --> 00:09:28,331
Um, well...

164
00:09:28,331 --> 00:09:30,831
I guess they're, um...

165
00:09:30,831 --> 00:09:32,491
They might be a little well-worn,

166
00:09:32,831 --> 00:09:34,231
but I'm a sucker for comfort.

167
00:09:34,331 --> 00:09:34,991
What can I say?

168
00:09:37,071 --> 00:09:39,411
Akutsu, first year of Asperion youth.

169
00:09:39,911 --> 00:09:41,071
It's nice to meet you.

170
00:09:41,571 --> 00:09:43,631
I'm Ashito Aoi, from Ehime.

171
00:09:43,631 --> 00:09:44,951
Okay, back at ya.

172
00:09:48,531 --> 00:09:50,331
So polite and well-mannered.

173
00:09:50,891 --> 00:09:53,551
Dang, I always pictured the youth team as elite.

174
00:09:54,051 --> 00:09:54,831
And I was right.

175
00:10:05,411 --> 00:10:05,931
What?

176
00:10:06,191 --> 00:10:06,771
No way.

177
00:10:07,071 --> 00:10:09,051
There's a huge blank space all of a sudden.

178
00:10:09,691 --> 00:10:10,611
Is it a trap?

179
00:10:11,051 --> 00:10:11,631
Aw, man.

180
00:10:13,631 --> 00:10:15,451
Otomo!

181
00:10:15,791 --> 00:10:16,091
Hey!

182
00:10:20,011 --> 00:10:21,691
No pressure, no marking.

183
00:10:22,051 --> 00:10:23,751
I'm slicing through them like butter.

184
00:10:24,331 --> 00:10:24,811
Aoi!

185
00:10:24,951 --> 00:10:25,911
Hm?

186
00:10:27,051 --> 00:10:27,411
Ah!

187
00:10:29,911 --> 00:10:31,211
That was so close!

188
00:10:31,211 --> 00:10:33,791
Did you see that?

189
00:10:33,891 --> 00:10:35,931
It only took three of them to break through their line.

190
00:10:44,971 --> 00:10:45,371
Otomo!

191
00:10:47,151 --> 00:10:49,091
He passed it in behind them again!

192
00:10:51,871 --> 00:10:53,051
Another close one!

193
00:10:53,051 --> 00:11:04,151
Do you even know how to play this game?

194
00:11:04,411 --> 00:11:05,531
How embarrassing!

195
00:11:05,971 --> 00:11:08,531
The youth team is supposed to be their inspiration!

196
00:11:09,651 --> 00:11:11,531
You're losing to the losers!

197
00:11:11,711 --> 00:11:12,591
Get it together!

198
00:11:12,591 --> 00:11:15,811
Are you okay?

199
00:11:16,411 --> 00:11:18,891
I got excited and gave myself a nosebleed.

200
00:11:22,391 --> 00:11:24,431
Are they trying to go easy on us?

201
00:11:25,511 --> 00:11:26,331
No way.

202
00:11:28,551 --> 00:11:29,491
What do you think?

203
00:11:29,851 --> 00:11:31,091
Are those the benchwarmers?

204
00:11:31,091 --> 00:11:35,631
Does that work?

205
00:11:36,311 --> 00:11:36,751
Yep.

206
00:11:37,171 --> 00:11:38,051
No problem.

207
00:11:43,431 --> 00:11:44,071
Great.

208
00:11:44,411 --> 00:11:45,051
Nice.

209
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:47,331
That was faster than I thought.

210
00:11:47,331 --> 00:12:07,771
They might play at a pro level, but they're not doing so hot today.

211
00:12:08,091 --> 00:12:09,611
Let's do this!

212
00:12:14,331 --> 00:12:15,431
Go, number 10!

213
00:12:15,811 --> 00:12:16,971
Breakthrough down the wing!

214
00:12:17,331 --> 00:12:19,071
Only one defender to beat.

215
00:12:19,391 --> 00:12:21,771
If I can get past him, I'll be right at the goal.

216
00:12:22,211 --> 00:12:24,991
I can use that first touch technique that the old man taught me.

217
00:12:25,691 --> 00:12:27,631
I'll land the ball right there.

218
00:12:27,991 --> 00:12:29,451
And he won't have any time to react.

219
00:12:32,011 --> 00:12:32,531
No!

220
00:12:32,831 --> 00:12:34,091
He got back already!

221
00:12:34,091 --> 00:12:55,971
Don't just stand there!

222
00:12:55,971 --> 00:12:57,171
Go and get the ball!

223
00:12:57,171 --> 00:12:59,231
Their passes are so accurate!

224
00:12:59,231 --> 00:13:00,411
Unbelievable!

225
00:13:00,411 --> 00:13:04,451
They're moving the ball around with only one touch passes!

226
00:13:04,451 --> 00:13:06,571
And barely any dribbling!

227
00:13:06,571 --> 00:13:10,451
Awesome, huh?

228
00:13:10,451 --> 00:13:13,391
I bet you're a little lost since you don't play, though.

229
00:13:13,391 --> 00:13:14,131
One touch passing.

230
00:13:14,131 --> 00:13:16,331
One touch passing.

231
00:13:16,331 --> 00:13:19,511
Pass the ball with a single touch.

232
00:13:19,711 --> 00:13:21,371
No trapping it or dribbling first.

233
00:13:21,371 --> 00:13:25,651
If they do it right, they can bear down on the other team's goal really fast.

234
00:13:25,651 --> 00:13:34,531
However, this style of play requires everyone involved to have exceptional passing, positioning, and the ability to calculate where the space will be.

235
00:13:34,531 --> 00:13:42,691
Meaning, in order to execute it successfully, all 11 of them must share a perfect mental map of the route the ball's going to take.

236
00:13:43,111 --> 00:13:44,111
That's unbelievable!

237
00:13:46,771 --> 00:13:48,451
Snap out of it, you idiot!

238
00:13:48,811 --> 00:13:50,771
Do you like getting outplayed like this?

239
00:13:50,851 --> 00:13:52,311
Because I sure as hell don't!

240
00:13:54,551 --> 00:13:56,011
For real this time!

241
00:13:57,611 --> 00:13:59,111
Take it down, End!

242
00:14:04,531 --> 00:14:09,691
That's it for the first half!

243
00:14:11,131 --> 00:14:13,471
This kind of thing doesn't happen in real life.

244
00:14:13,971 --> 00:14:16,471
I took the ball down and kicked it as soon as it landed?

245
00:14:16,991 --> 00:14:21,011
That means he knew exactly where I was trying to place it the entire time.

246
00:14:21,491 --> 00:14:22,891
Who is this guy?

247
00:14:24,891 --> 00:14:27,231
Hey, so about your cleats.

248
00:14:28,731 --> 00:14:30,791
Is it because you can't afford new ones?

249
00:14:30,791 --> 00:14:36,351
What's the big deal if I can't?

250
00:14:37,611 --> 00:14:39,471
I heard you traveled a long way.

251
00:14:40,071 --> 00:14:41,351
Must have been pretty expensive.

252
00:14:41,571 --> 00:14:42,611
Who paid for your trip?

253
00:14:45,611 --> 00:14:47,871
Something's out there for you, so go find it.

254
00:14:55,971 --> 00:14:58,411
It's sad to see such a lack of talent.

255
00:14:58,811 --> 00:14:59,691
Pathetic, really.

256
00:15:00,791 --> 00:15:02,531
I'm not talking about you.

257
00:15:03,731 --> 00:15:05,891
I mean the kids around you.

258
00:15:10,331 --> 00:15:13,091
Talentless losers talking about how hard this is for them.

259
00:15:14,011 --> 00:15:16,111
That's not going to make any friends out here.

260
00:15:16,671 --> 00:15:19,371
All you want to do is have fun playing soccer, right?

261
00:15:20,311 --> 00:15:21,211
Go home.

262
00:15:21,671 --> 00:15:22,991
We don't need that trash.

263
00:15:24,611 --> 00:15:26,891
This isn't some little playground, kid.

264
00:15:30,791 --> 00:15:35,731
Akutsu, you weren't running your mouth again, were you?

265
00:15:36,831 --> 00:15:39,711
I don't get it.

266
00:15:40,071 --> 00:15:42,411
Why didn't they do that one-touch passing from the start?

267
00:15:42,931 --> 00:15:45,291
I wonder if they did it just to mock us.

268
00:15:45,831 --> 00:15:47,811
Or maybe they were just showing off for the crowd.

269
00:15:49,151 --> 00:15:49,511
Hmm.

270
00:15:49,951 --> 00:15:51,811
It was pretty amazing, though.

271
00:15:51,811 --> 00:15:54,811
Come on, Lee.

272
00:15:55,631 --> 00:15:56,071
Hasegawa!

273
00:15:56,311 --> 00:15:57,191
What are you all doing?

274
00:15:57,691 --> 00:15:59,351
You want to join this meeting or what?

275
00:16:01,351 --> 00:16:04,051
Oh, hey.

276
00:16:04,191 --> 00:16:05,791
I haven't seen you guys since Inner High.

277
00:16:06,131 --> 00:16:06,971
Eisuku Otomo.

278
00:16:07,271 --> 00:16:08,151
You guys remember me?

279
00:16:08,691 --> 00:16:11,191
If you think you can put your skills to full use today,

280
00:16:11,311 --> 00:16:13,251
then we might not all have to go home.

281
00:16:13,251 --> 00:16:18,451
I sure don't want it to end like this.

282
00:16:18,751 --> 00:16:19,171
Do you?

283
00:16:28,971 --> 00:16:30,411
Get that thing away from me!

284
00:16:30,471 --> 00:16:31,191
What are you doing?

285
00:16:31,351 --> 00:16:32,931
Nobody asked you to come and play nurse!

286
00:16:33,871 --> 00:16:36,111
Don't underestimate me just because I'm pretty.

287
00:16:36,611 --> 00:16:37,771
I know what I'm doing.

288
00:16:38,151 --> 00:16:39,951
Stopping nosebleeds is super easy.

289
00:16:39,951 --> 00:16:47,311
Who the heck is she supposed to be again?

290
00:16:47,691 --> 00:16:50,391
She said something about being the old man's sister before.

291
00:16:50,911 --> 00:16:51,851
That's kind of weird.

292
00:16:59,191 --> 00:17:00,071
Pathetic, really.

293
00:17:00,391 --> 00:17:02,351
I mean the kids around you.

294
00:17:08,211 --> 00:17:08,691
Whoa!

295
00:17:08,691 --> 00:17:10,291
You need to hold still!

296
00:17:10,631 --> 00:17:11,531
You're too close!

297
00:17:11,651 --> 00:17:12,931
Personal space, man!

298
00:17:19,571 --> 00:17:20,511
That's Akutsu.

299
00:17:20,711 --> 00:17:21,671
Is he bothering you?

300
00:17:21,871 --> 00:17:23,591
I don't get what his problem is.

301
00:17:25,831 --> 00:17:27,191
Scary, isn't he?

302
00:17:27,611 --> 00:17:30,311
There are plenty of snobby elite-level players here.

303
00:17:30,851 --> 00:17:32,351
He's definitely the worst.

304
00:17:32,771 --> 00:17:35,271
And he's still a first-year, but he's already a starter.

305
00:17:35,271 --> 00:17:37,631
Another thing?

306
00:17:38,011 --> 00:17:40,911
He's the only member who made it in through last year's tryouts.

307
00:17:47,211 --> 00:17:49,671
He was in the same position I am now.

308
00:17:50,431 --> 00:17:52,811
Who is he to say if I have talent or not?

309
00:17:53,211 --> 00:17:55,791
He's gonna regret that stupid punk.

310
00:17:56,331 --> 00:17:56,991
Come on!

311
00:17:57,151 --> 00:17:59,151
Second half's starting and I want us to pass!

312
00:17:59,371 --> 00:18:01,491
Let's show them all how bad we can be!

313
00:18:01,491 --> 00:18:03,231
You got this!

314
00:18:04,731 --> 00:18:05,291
Wow.

315
00:18:05,731 --> 00:18:08,091
That huddle looks a lot bigger than it did before.

316
00:18:08,091 --> 00:18:28,931
That was like running into an iron wall!

317
00:18:29,431 --> 00:18:31,351
This guy's core strength is crazy!

318
00:18:31,351 --> 00:18:37,831
We're five minutes into the second half.

319
00:18:38,411 --> 00:18:42,171
They really haven't done anything difficult like the one-touch passing from the first half.

320
00:18:42,691 --> 00:18:43,851
They're keeping it simple.

321
00:18:44,611 --> 00:18:45,091
Or not.

322
00:18:50,351 --> 00:18:52,771
The youth team has some really talented players!

323
00:18:53,471 --> 00:18:54,111
What the heck?

324
00:18:54,591 --> 00:18:55,391
Is this real life?

325
00:18:55,911 --> 00:18:58,831
It's like they're totally different players than they were at the start of the game!

326
00:18:58,831 --> 00:19:01,791
Get over here!

327
00:19:02,151 --> 00:19:02,791
Back to me!

328
00:19:03,011 --> 00:19:03,371
You and I!

329
00:19:04,231 --> 00:19:05,831
Come on, you guys!

330
00:19:06,891 --> 00:19:07,651
Play on!

331
00:19:10,991 --> 00:19:13,611
That Kaneda's kind of a hothead, don't you think?

332
00:19:14,591 --> 00:19:15,351
Corner kick!

333
00:19:16,031 --> 00:19:17,231
Nice stop, Koly!

334
00:19:17,531 --> 00:19:18,291
Great job!

335
00:19:19,891 --> 00:19:22,271
It's shocking how useless you all are.

336
00:19:22,271 --> 00:19:26,111
All of a sudden you know how to play?

337
00:19:26,591 --> 00:19:28,731
Dude, what's that supposed to prove?

338
00:19:30,111 --> 00:19:32,531
It took us a while to warm up, I guess.

339
00:19:33,991 --> 00:19:40,251
Hey, before the second half kicked off, you were all standing in a circle and clapping.

340
00:19:40,691 --> 00:19:41,751
What was that about?

341
00:19:43,031 --> 00:19:45,791
Aren't you guys all here to compete against each other?

342
00:19:46,411 --> 00:19:46,931
Vomit.

343
00:19:46,931 --> 00:19:52,411
Is talking trash like that how you managed to pass last year's tryouts?

344
00:19:52,951 --> 00:19:53,971
Makes sense now.

345
00:19:54,911 --> 00:19:55,311
Hmm?

346
00:19:55,851 --> 00:19:56,771
You do you.

347
00:19:57,071 --> 00:19:59,471
But I don't have to be a douchebag in order to get in.

348
00:20:02,611 --> 00:20:03,931
Hey, you guys!

349
00:20:04,151 --> 00:20:05,691
Quit pouting or I'm gonna spit!

350
00:20:06,571 --> 00:20:07,751
It's a set play!

351
00:20:08,131 --> 00:20:09,151
We gotta defend!

352
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:11,171
Who are you marking, huh?

353
00:20:11,431 --> 00:20:11,771
Him?

354
00:20:12,011 --> 00:20:12,651
Or him?

355
00:20:13,011 --> 00:20:14,391
Um, we don't know.

356
00:20:14,391 --> 00:20:18,191
After that, I'll go score some goals!

357
00:20:18,391 --> 00:20:19,531
I need your help, alright?

358
00:20:19,811 --> 00:20:23,091
No matter where I am on the field, I need you to get the ball to me!

359
00:20:23,251 --> 00:20:23,931
Hey, you guys!

360
00:20:24,071 --> 00:20:24,891
Owie's got a point!

361
00:20:25,291 --> 00:20:27,311
We knew the youth team would be strong!

362
00:20:27,471 --> 00:20:29,331
We were bound to give up a few goals!

363
00:20:29,931 --> 00:20:30,351
Yeah!

364
00:20:30,791 --> 00:20:33,251
We gotta stay focused on playing our best game!

365
00:20:33,571 --> 00:20:34,251
Let's do it!

366
00:20:34,451 --> 00:20:35,871
It's not over till it's over!

367
00:20:35,871 --> 00:20:36,511
Hmm.

368
00:20:39,751 --> 00:20:40,231
Owie!

369
00:20:40,431 --> 00:20:40,791
Over there!

370
00:20:40,791 --> 00:20:41,271
Clear it!

371
00:20:41,351 --> 00:20:41,671
Yeah!

372
00:20:44,391 --> 00:20:58,731
I swear, I didn't mean it!

373
00:20:58,851 --> 00:21:00,831
I just lost my balance in midair!

374
00:21:01,231 --> 00:21:02,151
I'm so sorry!

375
00:21:02,271 --> 00:21:02,991
Are you okay?

376
00:21:03,931 --> 00:21:04,531
Yeah.

377
00:21:05,051 --> 00:21:05,911
I'm great.

378
00:21:05,911 --> 00:21:15,731
Can you move?

379
00:21:16,191 --> 00:21:17,331
Let's get you off the field.

380
00:21:19,991 --> 00:21:22,251
I could use a little help getting up here.

381
00:21:22,391 --> 00:21:23,411
Do you mind?

382
00:21:26,091 --> 00:21:28,211
I don't have time to be lying around.

383
00:21:28,331 --> 00:21:29,871
We've got a game to finish, right?

384
00:21:29,871 --> 00:21:36,231
Hey, are you sure you're okay, Owie?

385
00:21:36,451 --> 00:21:38,731
Come over to the sidelines so I can take a look!

386
00:21:38,851 --> 00:21:39,791
I don't need that.

387
00:21:40,351 --> 00:21:41,891
I just need to score goals.

388
00:21:42,271 --> 00:21:42,751
Please.

389
00:21:44,811 --> 00:21:46,811
I can't let it end like this.

390
00:21:47,031 --> 00:21:47,951
I need to stay.

391
00:21:48,211 --> 00:21:49,711
I can't go back home now!

392
00:21:51,311 --> 00:21:55,311
Dude, you actually think we let you leave before getting a chance to show you up?

393
00:21:55,531 --> 00:21:56,251
No way!

394
00:21:56,331 --> 00:21:57,091
Are you kidding?

395
00:21:57,091 --> 00:22:04,231
Hey, Fukuda, wait!

396
00:22:04,751 --> 00:22:05,651
Are you going to tell them?

397
00:22:06,271 --> 00:22:07,651
You think now's the best time?

398
00:22:08,231 --> 00:22:10,071
Now's as good a time as any, Nozomi.

399
00:22:14,091 --> 00:22:17,131
Uh, there's something you should know.

400
00:22:18,351 --> 00:22:22,251
During this game, I purposefully handicapped the youth team.

401
00:22:22,251 --> 00:22:27,871
With the exception of the goalie, everyone's playing a position they've never played before.

402
00:22:28,931 --> 00:22:31,391
So, you haven't played them at their best.

403
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:26,746
Next time on Awashi, Rope.

